diff --git a/CHANGELOG.en.md b/CHANGELOG.en.md
index 9ef710f..0c7ded4 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.en.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.en.md
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ Notable changes in Telsiz releases are listed in this file. Version numbers foll
 - The placeholder of the Add Friend field now reads "Enter a username" (before "username"). The field's label is only visible to screen readers, so the placeholder is the only visible hint.
 - The desktop app tells the page the window state and the system idle time. The page learns through `telsizDesktop.onWindowState` when the window is minimized, comes back from being minimized (including going back to full screen), is hidden to the tray and is shown again (including coming back from the tray). It reads the time since the last user input in whole seconds through `telsizDesktop.idleSeconds()`, and the background windows of frequencies that are not open read it through `telsizArkaPlan.idleSeconds()`. Only one of four state values reaches the page, and only the app window and background windows may read the idle time. These channels are the desktop groundwork for Telsiz DJ, the floating window and automatic idle, and make no visible change on their own.
 - In Telsiz DJ a new track, a track change and resuming are anchored 3 seconds ahead for YouTube tracks and 1.5 seconds ahead for audio files (before, every track was anchored 1.5 seconds ahead and resuming happened at once). Devices load during this time and start together from the same point. While a YouTube track is playing in the room, a person who has not allowed the YouTube player yet sees a notice with Load the YouTube Player and No, Don't Load It buttons on the radio card, and a short notification appears for every new YouTube track even while the DJ card is open. In the desktop app, a YouTube track pauses on this device when the window is minimized or hidden in the tray and resumes in sync with the room when the window comes back. Audio files play in a single audio element. While the DJ column is open, the stage layout is built with flexbox instead of a grid (it looks the same).
+- In Telsiz DJ the YouTube player stays in the same frame for the whole session in the voice room. When the track changes, the player is not rebuilt, the next video is prepared in the same player and starts together with the other devices in the room, so the player no longer has to load for every track. While an audio file plays, the player waits paused. The player is removed when the session ends, when the YouTube consent is withdrawn, when the YouTube source is turned off and when you leave the voice room. The intent is also to keep the permission to play that was given with a tap on a phone valid for the following tracks, which has not been tried with the real YouTube yet.
 
 ### Fixes
 
diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 1408f27..2cbc65b 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@ Telsiz'in sürümlerindeki önemli değişiklikler bu dosyada listelenir. Sürü
 - Arkadaş Ekle kutusunun yer tutucusu artık "Kullanıcı adı giriniz" (önceden "kullanici_adi"). Kutunun etiketi yalnızca ekran okuyucuya göründüğü için yer tutucu tek görünen ipucudur.
 - Masaüstü uygulaması sayfaya pencerenin durumunu ve sistemin boşta süresini bildirir. Sayfa pencerenin simge durumuna küçültüldüğünü, simge durumundan döndüğünü (tam ekrana dönüş dahil), tepsiye gizlendiğini ve yeniden gösterildiğini (tepsiden dönüş dahil) `telsizDesktop.onWindowState` ile öğrenir. Son kullanıcı girişinden bu yana geçen süreyi tam saniye olarak `telsizDesktop.idleSeconds()` ile, açık olmayan frekansların arka plan pencereleri `telsizArkaPlan.idleSeconds()` ile okur. Sayfaya yalnızca dört durum değerinden biri gider, boşta süresini yalnızca uygulama penceresi ve arka plan pencereleri okuyabilir. Bu kanallar Telsiz DJ, yüzen pencere ve otomatik boşta için masaüstü altyapısıdır, kendi başlarına görünür bir değişiklik yapmaz.
 - Telsiz DJ'de yeni parça, parça geçişi ve devam ettirme YouTube parçasında 3, ses dosyasında 1,5 saniye ileri çapalanır (önceden her parça 1,5 saniye, devam ettirme hemen). Cihazlar bu sürede yükler ve aynı yerden birlikte başlar. YouTube oynatıcısına henüz izin vermemiş kişi, odada YouTube parçası çalarken telsiz kartında YouTube Oynatıcısını Yükle ve Hayır, Yükleme düğmeli bir uyarı görür, her yeni YouTube parçasında DJ kartı açıkken de kısa bir bildirim çıkar. Masaüstü uygulamasında pencere simge durumuna küçültülünce veya tepsiye gizlenince YouTube parçası bu cihazda duraklar, pencere geri gelince odayla eşitlenip sürer. Ses dosyaları tek bir ses öğesinde çalar. DJ sütunu açıkken sahnenin düzeni ızgara yerine flexbox ile kurulur (görünüm aynı).
+- Telsiz DJ'de YouTube oynatıcısı ses odasındaki oturum boyunca aynı çerçevede kalır. Parça değişince oynatıcı yeniden kurulmaz, sonraki video aynı oynatıcıda hazırlanır ve odadaki diğer cihazlarla birlikte başlar, böylece her parçada oynatıcının yüklenmesi beklenmez. Dosya parçası çalarken oynatıcı duraklatılmış bekler. Oynatıcı oturum bitince, YouTube izni geri alınınca, YouTube kaynağı kapanınca ve ses odasından çıkınca kaldırılır. Telefonda dokunarak verilen oynatma izninin sonraki parçalarda da geçerli kalması amaçlanır, bu gerçek YouTube ile henüz denenmedi.
 
 ### Düzeltmeler
 
diff --git a/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md b/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
index 0ba176d..7c0232f 100644
--- a/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
+++ b/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
@@ -168,6 +168,8 @@ The server (`src/music.js`) keeps this envelope only in memory and cannot see it
 
 Each device plays the music in its own player and computes the position from the anchor. A new track, a track change and resuming are anchored ahead by a start lead: 3 seconds for YouTube tracks and 1.5 seconds for audio files. Devices load during this time and start at the same moment from the same position. If the drift exceeds 1.5 seconds, the position is corrected silently. Shared audio files are encrypted uploads like message attachments and are decrypted and played on the device. YouTube tracks play in the official YouTube embedded player inside an isolated frame from the `youtube-nocookie.com` origin. No Google code runs in the app's own origin, and the YouTube API scripts are not loaded. The frame is never loaded before the person gives consent on that device, and the consent can be withdrawn in Settings > Privacy and security.
 
+A single YouTube frame is used for the whole session in the voice room. When the track changes, the frame is not rebuilt: the new video is prepared in the same frame with the IFrame Player API's `cueVideoById` command (the video loads but does not play) and the devices start it at the shared anchor. This way the frame's loading time is not paid again for every track. The intent is also to carry the permission to play that the person gave with a tap in the frame over to the following tracks, which has not been tried on a phone with the real YouTube yet. Messages about the old video that are still on their way when the command is sent (position, duration, name, playing or ended state) are not written to the new track: they are ignored until the frame reports the video cued or unstarted state or the new video's ID, for at most 1.5 seconds. While an audio file plays, the frame waits paused and its events go to no track. The frame is removed when the session ends (no track is left to play), when the consent is withdrawn, when the YouTube source or Telsiz DJ is turned off, when the person leaves the voice room or moves to another voice room, and when the player area changes. If the player reported an error or is not ready yet, the next track opens in a new frame. The frame's origin, its sandbox flags, the origin and source checks on incoming messages and the consent rule do not change.
+
 Audio file tracks play in a single `<audio>` element for the lifetime of the engine, and only the source address changes when the track changes. The interface draws the card right away on the engine's track and state events. While the page is hidden (a background tab, a minimized window) the browser holds back animation frames, so drawing is done with a timer, and the YouTube player area is drawn at least 200x200 in the background too and the track starts together with the other devices. When the card is not visible, the player is moved to one of the four corners and can be minimized. The engine's local hold (a minimized player, a minimized window or a window hidden in the tray reported in the desktop app by `telsizDesktop.onWindowState`, Pause in the system's media controls) only stops the player on that device and does not change the shared state. When the hold is released, the player jumps to the shared position. The hold from Pause in the media controls is lifted when the person leaves the voice room. The bar of the player in the corner shows a hold the person can release (media controls, minimize), and while it is active the bar's button does not pause the room and only releases the hold. A YouTube track is not played while its player is not visible, and the minimize and window holds apply only to YouTube tracks.
 
 When a track is added, the client of the person adding it sends an encrypted announcement message to the text room. The `d` field in the plaintext of the message is `{ op: 'add', src: 'yt', vid, title }`, `{ op: 'add', src: 'file', title }` for an audio file attached to the same message (`/play` with an attachment), or `{ op: 'add', src: 'fileref', title }` for an audio file in another message added with "Play in DJ". `title` is optional, the receiver removes control and direction characters from it and shortens it to at most 120 code points, and older clients ignore the field. A `fileref` announcement has no attachment. Older clients that do not know this source ignore the `d` field and show the text of the message, so the text of that announcement is the full translated announcement. The name of a YouTube track may not be known when it is added, and the first device that loads its player writes the name into the DJ state. The person adding waits up to 8 seconds, if no name arrives or the page is hidden or closed in the meantime the announcement goes out without it, and once the name arrives the person adding edits their own message. The server only checks the author of an edit, cannot see the body and does not keep its earlier version. So the edited label is only hidden for an edit the client followed in the open conversation and compared with the earlier version: the earlier version is a DJ announcement without a name that was never edited, the new version only adds the name with the same source and video, and the edit is made within 10 minutes of sending the announcement (with one minute allowed for delay). An edit whose earlier version is not known (the conversation was opened later, the page was reloaded) and every other edit shows the label.
